# Flyball sound circuits -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Ryan Holtz's netlist of the sound circuits on the game board, which his file says is
# derived from the schematics in the manual. The game logic's sound-enable and sound-data
# lines arrive as ports (MAME's TTL_INPUT names), and so do the video timing signals the
# sounds are clocked from, which MAME runs as ideal clocks.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/atari/nl_flyball.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(flyball). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Ryan Holtz (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/atari/nl_flyball.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 73: dropped NET_C(VCC, IC_E7.14, IC_B7.14, IC_C7.14, IC_D7.14, IC_E7.13, IC_B7.9, IC_B7.2, IC_C7.9, IC_C7.2) -- took IC_E7.13, IC_B7.9, IC_B7.2, IC_C7.9, IC_C7.2 out of it: sheet 7 pulls E7.13 up through R25, and draws B7 and C7 pins 2 and 9 as bare stubs
# line 91: dropped NET_C(VCC, IC_D7.13, IC_D7.1) -- took IC_D7.1 out of it: sheet 7 pulls D7.1 up through R25
# line 111: dropped NET_C(V5, IC_E7.2, R73.1, R74.1) -- took IC_E7.2 out of it: sheet 7 pulls E7.2 up through R25
#
# Corrected from sheet 7 of the schematic (005629 rev A, TM-075 pp. 56-57):
#   parts the sheet draws that MAME does not have: R25 1K
#   sheet 7: the pull-up R25 ('P,R25') on D7.1, E7.2 and E7.13: V5 R25.1
#   as above: R25.2 UD7.1 UE7.2 UE7.13
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): CLOCK(H256), CLOCK(V128), TTL_INPUT(BAT_SOUND), TTL_INPUT(FOOTSTEP), TTL_INPUT(CROWD_SL), TTL_INPUT(CROWD_ON), TTL_INPUT(CROWD_VL)
#
# Compared with the schematic, sheet 7 of 9 'Sound Generator' (005629 rev A, TM-075 pp.
# 56-57, the sheet scanned in two halves), with parts list A005629-01 (pp. 62-65), on
# 2026-10-20: 39 of MAME's 41 nets agree pin for pin -- the noise generator (all ten of its
# connections), the band-pass filter, the bat sound's 556, the footstep envelope, the crowd
# and whistle control and the mixer -- and the supplies are as MAME has them (+18V, an
# unregulated rail, on A8, C8 and D8). Corrected above from the sheet: D7.1, E7.2 and E7.13
# go to +5V through the 1K pull-up R25, which MAME leaves out, and B7 and C7 pins 2 and 9
# (B gate and CLR) are drawn as bare stubs, which MAME ties to +5V -- an open TTL input
# floats high, the level the circuit needs, so the board may tie them, but the drawing does
# not. D7.13 is drawn 'P', an unnamed pull-up, and is left on +5V here.
#
# Kept as MAME has them, each against the sheet: R79 is 820K on the sheet and the parts list
# and 1K in MAME, whose comment says 'Verified as 1K on a real board'; R97B (24.4K, in
# parallel with R97) is on neither, and MAME's comment says it was 'verified to exist on a
# real board'; C46/C47 are .01 on the sheet and .015 on the parts list, which MAME follows;
# R80 is 330K on the sheet and 330 ohms on the parts list, and MAME follows the sheet. A8 and
# C8 are printed 'MFC3340P' with the MFC6040's pin numbers in brackets beside each pin, and
# the parts list fits MFC6040s, with the MFC3340 as the substitute 'when stock of MFC6040 is
# depleted'; this file is the MFC3340 wiring, so a board carrying MFC6040s has the bracketed
# pins instead (as Tank's do). E7's fourth gate (4, 5, 6), which MAME grounds, is not on
# sheet 7, and the output amplifier (the TDA1004 at B9) is on it and not in MAME.

# part UA8 MC3340
# part UB7 74164
# part UC7 74164
# part UC8 MC3340
# part UD7 7474
# part UD8 UA741
# part UE7 7486
# part UE8 NE556

value R25 1K
value R43 68K
value R73 1K
value R74 1K
value R76 100K
value R77 820
value R78 100K
value R79 1K  # MAME's comment: 'RES., CARBON, 5%, 1/4W, 820K // Verified as 1K on a real board'
value R80 330K  # MAME's comment: 'RES., CARBON, 5%, 1/4W, 330 // (330 on parts list, but 330K on schematic, 330 does not work in the netlist)'
value R87 1K
value R88 3.3K
value R89 10K
value R90 10K
value R91 10K
value R92 10K
value R96 47K
value R97A 10K
value R97B 24.4K  # MAME's comment: 'RES., CARBON, 5%, 1/4W, 10K // Verified to exist on a real board'
value R98 10K
value R99 33K
value R75 50K
value R95 10K
value C34 0.0047uF
value C44 0.0047uF
value C45 0.1uF
value C46 0.015uF
value C47 0.015uF
value C48 10uF
value C49 100uF
value C51 0.1uF
value C52 0.1uF
value C53 0.1uF
value C79 0.1uF
value C80 0.1uF

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C34.2 C44.2 C45.2 C48.2 C49.2 C51.2 C52.2 UA8.3 UB7.7 UC7.7 UC8.3 UD7.2 UD7.7 UD8.4 UE7.4 UE7.5 UE7.7 UE8.7 R77.2 R95.1
net +18V: UA8.8 UC8.8 UD8.7
net +5V: UB7.14 UC7.14 UD7.13 UD7.14 UD8.3 UE7.14 UE8.14 R25.1 R73.1 R74.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UD7.1 UE7.13 UE7.2 R25.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Random Noise Generator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port H256: UB7.8 UC7.8 UD7.11 UD7.4  # in MAME: CLOCK(H256)
wire UB7.13 UC7.1
wire UC7.13 UD7.12
wire UD7.9 UE7.9
wire UB7.5 UE7.10
wire UE7.12 UE7.8
wire UB7.1 UE7.11
wire UD7.10 UD7.5
port V128: UD7.3  # in MAME: CLOCK(V128)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Band Pass Filter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UD7.8 R78.1 R79.1
wire C46.1 C47.1 R77.1 R78.2
wire C46.2 UD8.6 R80.1 R87.1
wire C47.2 UD8.2 R80.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bat Sound
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port BAT_SOUND: UE7.1 UE8.10 UE8.4  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(BAT_SOUND)
wire UE8.1 R74.2 R75.2 R75.3
wire R43.1 R75.1
wire C34.1 UE8.2 UE8.6 R43.2
wire UE8.13 R73.2 R76.1
wire C44.1 UE8.12 UE8.8 R76.2
wire C45.1 UE8.11 UE8.3
wire UE8.5 R91.1
wire UE8.9 R90.1
wire UE7.3 R89.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Footstep Envelope Generator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port FOOTSTEP: R88.1  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(FOOTSTEP)
wire C79.1 R79.2
wire C79.2 UC8.1
wire C48.1 UC8.2 R88.2
wire UC8.7 R92.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crowd & Whistle Volume Control
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C80.1 R87.2
wire C80.2 UA8.1
port CROWD_VL: R97A.2 R97B.2  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(CROWD_VL)
port CROWD_ON: R98.2  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(CROWD_ON)
port CROWD_SL: R99.2  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(CROWD_SL)
wire C49.1 UA8.2 R97A.1 R97B.1 R98.1 R99.1
wire UA8.7 R96.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mixer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C51.1 R89.2 R90.2 R91.2 R92.2 R95.3 R96.2
wire C53.1 R95.2
port OUTPUT: C52.1 C53.2  # on to the audio amplifier, which MAME does not simulate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
nc UA8.6  # line 152: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC8.6  # line 153: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.2  # line 154: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.9  # line 155: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.3  # line 156: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.4  # line 157: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.6  # line 158: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.10  # line 159: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.11  # line 160: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UB7.12  # line 161: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.3  # line 162: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.4  # line 163: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.5  # line 164: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.6  # line 165: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.10  # line 166: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.11  # line 167: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UC7.12  # line 168: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UD7.6  # line 169: MAME's own HINT(NC)
nc UE7.6  # line 170: MAME's own HINT(NC)
# Pins the MAME netlist never mentions. On a real board these are unused outputs, or
# inputs left open or tied in a way MAME did not draw; they are written here so that
# the checker's coverage test still means something for every other pin.
nc UA8.4 UA8.5  # NC NC
nc UC7.2 UC7.9  # DSB ~{MR}
nc UC8.4 UC8.5  # NC NC
nc UD8.1 UD8.5 UD8.8  # NULL NULL NC
